Abstract = {This paper describes the Sargantana System on chip (SoC), a 64-bit
   RISC-V single core processor designed by a number of academic
   institutions and manufactured in 22 nm FDSOI technology: BSC, UPC, UB,
   UAB, CIC-IPN and IMB-CNM (CSIC). The SoC includes the processor as well
   as, among other components, a Phase Locked Loop (PLL) operating up to 2
   GHz, interfaces to HyperRAM and a Serdes up to 8 Gbps. The processor has
   demonstrated experimental correct operation at 800 MHz.},
