   FRONTIERS 2023, CF 2023},
Year = {2023},
Pages = {387-388},
Note = {20th ACM International Conference on Computing Frontiers (CF), Bologna,
   ITALY, MAY 09-11, 2023},
Abstract = {With an ever increasing utilization of open-source hardware, the demand
   for improved productivity in its various development phases rises. This
   demand can only be met by open-source tools accompanying these
   open-hardware projects to cover their crucial tasks in design, test, and
   verification. One of these required tasks is fault injection analysis.
   At early stages of development, it can help to identify vulnerabilities
   of the hardware designs. In this work, we propose the open-source tool
   vRTLmod which enables low overhead and scaling fault injection
   simulations at Register Tranfer Level (RTL).},
